[size=6][b]The Longest Year[/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Restore the Community Center within a single year — or the Junimos rewind the seasons and you begin again, a little stronger.[/i][/size]

[color=yellow][b]BETA (0.12.0-beta.1).[/b] Feature-complete and stable in testing. What it needs now is your feedback on difficulty, pricing, and pacing — see the bottom of this page.[/color]

[line]

[size=5][b]What's New in 0.12.0-beta.1[/b][/size]
[b]The mod now builds the Community Center board itself — and ten of the bugs you reported on 0.11.60 are fixed.[/b]
[list]
[*][b]A new board every loop.[/b] Each rewind rolls a fresh set of bundles from the vanilla [i]and[/i] remix pools plus eleven new authored ones — Gil's Trophies (donate eradication rewards, Warrior Ring included), Orchard, Four Seasons Sampler (Tea Saplings), Preserver's, Home Cook's Feast, Weatherman's, Recycler's and more. Picked bundles re-roll their contents from the game's own data (crops keep their season but can ask for anything season-valid; fish stay in their habitat), so it's SVE-proof and no two runs match. Weapons and hats can now be donated where a bundle asks for them. Vault asks are +25%.
[*][b]Remixed bundles no longer turn vanilla after a reset[/b] — the board is the mod's own now, so the farm-creation choice doesn't matter.
[*][b]The Community Center ceremony plays again[/b] after you finish the Center (Joja closes, Pierre opens Wednesdays, the lightning strikes). We had the wrong event suppressed.
[*][b]Museum rewards return every loop[/b] — Ancient Seeds + recipe, the statues, the Singing Stone.
[*][b]Caroline's Tea Sapling event replays[/b] after a reset.
[*][b]Mixed Seeds finally roll Red Cabbage / Starfruit[/b] with the Cultivation upgrades (and Summer Seeds stop growing cabbage).
[*][b]Weather:[/b] Rain Totems, CJB and console weather work again, and seasons have real variety — the 2-rain / 2-storm / 2-snow minimums are guaranteed, every other day is rolled per loop at vanilla-like odds.
[*][b]Junimo Stash keeps day-28 deposits.[/b] Kept coops/barns come back [b]with their hay hopper[/b]. Kept rods keep their [b]bait and tackle[/b] (kept tools keep enchantments).
[*][b]A fail-night overnight event can no longer swallow the rewind[/b] and drop you on Summer 1.
[*][b]Economy:[/b] season checkpoints now award JP (150/250/400), donation JP is paid once, and a new [i]xp multiplier[/i] upgrade family (×2–×5 per skill, plus a ×10 capstone).
[*][b]Traveling Cart:[/b] the one-item cart is explained in-game on your first visit, and [font=Courier New]LimitTravelingCartStock[/font] turns the cap off if you'd rather have the full cart.
[/list]
Beta caveat: flipping [font=Courier New]EnableNonObjectDonations[/font] off mid-loop can leave an in-flight Gil's Trophies bundle un-donatable until the next reset.

Full history in [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/TheLongestYear/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[line]

[size=5][b]What it is[/b][/size]
The Longest Year turns Stardew's first year into a roguelite loop. Each season, you must give back enough of the land's bounty to the old Community Center hall. Fall short by a season's end and the Junimos turn time back to Spring 1 — the world resets, but the strength you've earned, and the power your offerings have banked, can carry forward. Restore the whole Center inside one year to break the loop for good.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Seasonal time-loop.[/b] Each season has a donation minimum. Miss it and the year unwinds to Spring 1.
[*][b]Junimo Points.[/b] Donations earn JP — scaled by rarity and by how late in the year you give. JP banks across loops.
[*][b]The Junimo Shrine.[/b] Spend JP on upgrades that let you hold on to some of what you gained: skill levels, tool tiers, recipes, buildings, a kept pet, and more.
[*][b]Weekly themes.[/b] Each week, pick a theme that grants a bonus and a paired liability. Plan around it.
[*][b]Carryover surfaces.[/b] A Bundle Log book that tracks each season's goals, a Cookbook and Craftbook to bank recipes, and a Junimo Stash chest that survives resets.
[*][b]A real intro.[/b] Lewis greets you on the porch; a Junimo explains the loop. Then the run begins.
[*][b]A starved Traveling Cart.[/b] Joja has squeezed the merchant's suppliers — the cart carries [b]one item[/b] per visit until you unlock more stalls with the [b]Cart Stall[/b] upgrades (and Cart Whisperer previews what's coming). Prefer the full vanilla cart? Turn off [font=Courier New]LimitTravelingCartStock[/font].
[*][b]Break the loop.[/b] Finish the Center in a year to win — then keep playing or start fresh.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Stardew Valley 1.6+ (PC)
[*]SMAPI 4.0.0+
[*]A [b]new save[/b] on the [b]Standard farm[/b]
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install SMAPI 4.0.0 or newer.
[*]Unzip into your [font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/Mods[/font] folder.
[*]Launch through SMAPI and [b]start a new game on the Standard farm[/b]. Farm-type and intro options are handled for you.
[*]Bundles are the mod's own: every loop rolls a fresh board from the vanilla + remix pools plus the mod's authored bundles, so the Standard/Remixed choice at farm creation doesn't matter.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Limitations (beta)[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]PC only — no Android port yet.
[*]Standard farm only.
[*]A run can only be started from a new game (other saves load normally and are left untouched).
[*]Intro cutscene and dialogue are a first pass.
[*]Multiplayer untested.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Tuning[/b][/size]
Everything difficulty-related lives in [font=Courier New]config.json[/font] — JP values, per-season multipliers, completion bonuses, starting gold, and per-bundle quotas. Tweak freely and tell me what felt right. [font=Courier New]LimitTravelingCartStock[/font] (also in GMCM) turns the one-item Traveling Cart cap off if you'd rather have the full vanilla cart.

[line]

[size=5][b]Feedback wanted[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Difficulty[/b] — are the seasonal minimums fair? Which wall hit hardest?
[*][b]Pricing[/b] — do JP earnings and shrine costs feel balanced? What did you save for first?
[*][b]Pacing[/b] — how many loops before it "clicked"? Did carryover make later loops feel stronger?
[*][b]Bugs[/b] — please attach your [font=Courier New]SMAPI-latest.txt[/font] (from [font=Courier New]Stardew Valley/ErrorLogs/[/font]).
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]Art wanted[/b][/size]
The mod leans on vanilla sprites throughout. If anyone would enjoy making some custom book/sprite artwork (the Cookbook and Craftbook especially), I'd genuinely love to accept it and credit you. Drop a note in the comments.

[i]Banner art by [b]cwybabiesucks[/b] — thank you![/i]

[line]

[size=5][b]Translations[/b][/size]
As of 0.11.60, every player-visible string in the mod lives in a JSON file ([font=Courier New]i18n/default.json[/font]) — the mod is fully translatable with no DLL edits or rebuilds. See [url=https://github.com/sonofskywalker3/TheLongestYear/blob/master/docs/TRANSLATING.md]TRANSLATING.md[/url] for how to add a language. If you translate it, let us know (Nexus DM or GitHub issue) and we'll link your work from the mod page.

